<title>ESTONIA: PUBLIC OFFER SET FOR EESTI GAAS, OLUMPIA.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC OFFER SET FOR EESTI GAAS, OLUMPIA.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The privatisation agency decided on Wednesday to sell the state's minority stake in Eesti Gaas and the Hotel Olumpia in a public offer set for June 30 to July 18, Economy Minister Jaak Leimann said.  </p>
<p>The agency decided earlier to sell a 12.33 percent stake in Eesti Gaas, 25.06 percent of Hotel Olumpia and 24 percent of metalworking firm Esmeta.</p>
<p>German Ruhrgas and Russian Gazprom already own around 45 percent of Eesti Gaas.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
